"9574df1c-44a5-59df-974a-c34c608e896d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cap " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488771} {:answer/id #uuid "f54c79d8-5b80-5135-8fbf-2f4df986e61d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cup " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488990} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9d5cf43-46d1-5177-8e2d-2002b8fcbaa2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "62541dad-de47-58c3-a80c-47be806ee721" :question/math-academy-id "q-235959" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d46569e841a4bd7cf6646788f7bb5aec88a2386f96b8614ffec3e9c055bc200.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\n$\\,$  The range is $f(x)\\in $\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [-3,0)$ is $[0,2)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [0,3]$ is $[-3,-1]$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-3,-1]\\cup [0,2).$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the value $y=2$ is NOT a valid output of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at this endpoint."} :step/id #uuid "272370e5-078e-580c-b640-0e722fe6c08f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489351}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489316 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9332e63-1cab-5470-8b68-c1ecfc21ab7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488921}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488921} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b880c10-d001-52e8-a071-fcae3bbfd587" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd0e570e-08e5-5524-96a6-7ec3e36a900c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488855} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a9fea34-4574-5f69-af39-751014ba8f68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489084} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3888f44-8f46-55f7-b16c-49957fec7733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488944}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488944} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ec1b407-4fc4-5513-801c-a4b1e6cc64a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2eb98296-341b-5be8-a509-1dce3cf14c43" :question/math-academy-id "q-236001" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9c69a1ff6845f4be53f42e166a682baf804919ccba0f344ccdd38bc249584efc.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $-3.$ This occurs when $x=1.$\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $0.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-3$ and $0,$ including $-3$ but not including $0.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-3\\le y<0,$ which can also be written as  $-3\\le f(x)<0.$"} :step/id #uuid "4667bb2a-2002-535b-abeb-65e5c33b3eb7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489362}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489351 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53d33833-5d73-5cd1-aaa3-ebbde8ba8d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488630}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488630} :answer-field/id #uuid "230144b7-3e1c-5d00-a4ef-98175b07993a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ad29ad-17ec-5062-a971-d2e903f99dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488521}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488521} :answer-field/id #uuid "24135b41-8d9b-5bb6-b1a6-3b7dacf56dbb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d6d2512-b6ad-5e4c-a557-45ccf9fd3ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488650}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488650} :answer-field/id #uuid "a54f849e-6d30-5e86-8655-07915a3cbd2f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "49c672a2-d467-5f34-bcf7-e5d722eb09ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-235999" :question/problem "![](images/ac/acf26785a0591659fb6c2d9ef906614f8c282a31fcf6e06d1718477c4c6aba38.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $-1.$ This occurs when $x\\to \\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $3.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note that this point is not included in the graph.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-1$ and $3,$ not including $-1$ and $3.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-1<y<3,$ which can also be written as $-1<f(x)<3.$"} :step/id #uuid "aba196a5-a956-50e2-b8a6-61106b7dc46b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489316}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489362 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151cd673-35b1-5901-b1e4-3f2f71811a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488517} :answer-field/id #uuid "af246519-227d-5a39-92f0-c9fb3022be21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c165e391-96c0-5f1a-8559-109c7f748bfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488861} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4799eb0-92e5-5e8a-a05b-b1fc23cc5f4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59ae91eb-e7d1-5b05-ab82-7c77711c0e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488641}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488641} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbbd8104-f926-5b39-b3f0-4089b321c8ec" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2636e2eb-9d96-5c30-898f-0b55c9dd4bbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-236386" :question/problem "![](images/20/20cf8d018f748534720eb3efe21c4adf9354a015d824dcc15bfd9c33ad14a895.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}\n$<f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs when $x\\to -\\infty .$ However, note  that this point is not included in the graph.\n\n- There is no largest $y$-value.\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $1$ and $\\infty ,$ but not including $1.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $1<y<\\infty ,$ which can also be written as \n$1<f(x)<\\infty .$"} :step/id #uuid "ceb88876-37e1-5b22-af2a-9cf0a535596a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489363}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489363 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e1d5456-f9d4-5149-86a2-9ba9a7c28a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488725}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488725} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b650656-bd36-5828-a479-5f52c0e48b4b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2520b781-4fa8-5f19-abe9-c773ef419534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488546} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b7ed819-da82-5a1b-a80b-815d82f58698" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "273427b6-1181-5cc4-9482-efd6c25dd700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488554}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488554} :answer-field/id #uuid "7167fd1b-94c1-5af4-adca-6b79f3ab33a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "92babace-3fcf-5d4a-8789-c7e1f3a12026" :question/math-academy-id "q-236716" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a837faad775bb111760b2e90920c0490c42473c77f74f8be7a46271df154d97.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?\n\nThe range is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)<$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "We find the ranges of the individual pieces and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-3,1)$ is $(-1,3)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in [1,4)$ is $\\{1\\}$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $(-1,3)\\cup \\{1\\}=(-1,3),$ which can also be written as \n\n$$\n-1<f(x)<3.\n$$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=-1$ and $y=3$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use \"less than\" $(<)$ instead of \"less than or equal to\" $(\\le )$ at these endpoints."} :step/id #uuid "cf6a1dfd-5754-5ce6-84a6-e24b8966c20d"}] :activity/title "The Range of a Function: Advanced Cases" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488449}]}
